      "content": "When a mechanical sed/perl pass over a grep-derived file list needs to insert literal `/` characters (e.g. a sentence naming a file path like `hooks/foo.sh`), perl's `-pe 's/old/new/'` with `/` as both delimiter and content character will fail to compile with cryptic 'unknown regexp modifier' errors. Use a small Python script with `str.replace()` (asserting exactly one occurrence per file before writing) instead -- it avoids delimiter collision entirely and is still a single scripted pass over one file list, preserving the 'never file-by-file by hand' intent.",
